<title>JAPAN: Nippon Oil wins rights to Mexican Gulf oil blocks.</title>
<headline>Nippon Oil wins rights to Mexican Gulf oil blocks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Oil Co Ltd said on Wednesday that it had jointly acquired exploration rights to five offshore oil blocks in the Gulf of Mexico, and plans to start a geophysical survey at some of the fields next year.</p>
<p>Nippon Oil teamed up in the bidding with some foreign firms, including Coastal Corp and British-Borneo Petroleum Syndicate Plc, a Nippon Oil spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Japanese refiner already operates 10 offshore gas fields in the Gulf of Mexico, producing 43 million cubic feet of natural gas per day, the spokesman added.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities +81-3-3432-8837</p>
